WEBVTT

1
00:00:28.583 --> 00:00:32.666
After introducing the three gunas –

2
00:00:32.666 --> 00:00:36.416
sattva, rajas, and tamas –

3
00:00:36.416 --> 00:00:39.625
Lord Krishna now explains how these gunas

4
00:00:39.625 --> 00:00:41.666
affect and bind

5
00:00:41.666 --> 00:00:43.416
the jivatma.

6
00:00:43.416 --> 00:00:44.250
In this verse

7
00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:47.625
He describes the characteristics of 
sattva Guna –

8
00:00:47.625 --> 00:00:51.416
and its binding effects.

9
00:00:51.416 --> 00:00:55.541
Although sattva is considered purer
than the other gunas

10
00:00:55.541 --> 00:00:59.000
and gives knowledge and happiness,

11
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.000
it still binds the jivatma.

12
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:02.833
This verse

13
00:01:02.833 --> 00:01:05.875
reveals this subtle danger –

14
00:01:05.875 --> 00:01:08.125
when the jivatma becomes attached

15
00:01:08.125 --> 00:01:10.625
to the knowledge and happiness
arising from sattva,

16
00:01:10.625 --> 00:01:15.708
that very attachment keeps it far
from true liberation.

17
00:01:20.166 --> 00:01:25.583
Lord Krishna addresses Arjun
as Anagha – sinless

18
00:01:25.583 --> 00:01:27.083
indicating that Arjun

19
00:01:27.083 --> 00:01:29.541
is truly free from the bondages

20
00:01:29.541 --> 00:01:31.125
in which ordinary people

21
00:01:31.125 --> 00:01:33.583
become bound through sattva Guna.

22
00:01:33.583 --> 00:01:37.458
Sattva Guna is called prakashaka
and anamaya –

23
00:01:37.458 --> 00:01:39.708
This means a person under its influence

24
00:01:39.708 --> 00:01:42.000
thinks with clarity,

25
00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:47.208
develops a desire for knowledge,
and maintains a calm mind.

26
00:01:47.208 --> 00:01:48.416
Such a person is drawn

27
00:01:48.416 --> 00:01:50.041
toward virtuous actions

28
00:01:50.041 --> 00:01:53.000
and avoids wrongdoing.

29
00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:54.833
They experience peace

30
00:01:54.833 --> 00:01:57.625
and contentment from within.

31
00:01:57.625 --> 00:02:01.125
But here a subtle danger is hidden.

32
00:02:01.125 --> 00:02:04.291
Sattva Guna gives happiness and knowledge,

33
00:02:04.291 --> 00:02:05.583
but binds the soul

34
00:02:05.583 --> 00:02:10.083
through attachment to that very
happiness and knowledge.

35
00:02:10.083 --> 00:02:11.750
As it is said –

36
00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:16.625
“sukha-sangena badhnati
jnana-sangena canagha”.

37
00:02:16.625 --> 00:02:19.916
Such a person gradually begins to think –

38
00:02:19.916 --> 00:02:21.125
‘I am wise,

39
00:02:21.125 --> 00:02:23.125
I am superior to others.’

40
00:02:23.125 --> 00:02:25.458
This subtle pride keeps them bound

41
00:02:25.458 --> 00:02:28.291
in the cycle of birth and death.

42
00:02:28.291 --> 00:02:31.500
They are unable to go beyond material gunas.

43
00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:33.666
A person influenced by sattva Guna

44
00:02:33.666 --> 00:02:37.458
may become a philosopher, scientist, or thinker.

45
00:02:37.458 --> 00:02:39.416
They feel their pursuit of deep

46
00:02:39.416 --> 00:02:42.291
knowledge elevates them.

47
00:02:42.291 --> 00:02:45.333
But this too is a form of bondage –

48
00:02:45.333 --> 00:02:48.750
it keeps the soul tied to the world.

49
00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.541
A being bound by sattva Guna
experiences high knowledge

50
00:02:51.541 --> 00:02:53.708
and happiness,

51
00:02:53.708 --> 00:02:56.416
yet is not liberated.

52
00:02:56.416 --> 00:02:59.708
True liberation is beyond all gunas.

53
00:02:59.708 --> 00:03:03.333
It comes only through pure devotion.

54
00:03:03.333 --> 00:03:04.875
This is why Lord Krishna

55
00:03:04.875 --> 00:03:07.041
cautions Arjun

56
00:03:07.041 --> 00:03:08.833
that even sattva Guna,

57
00:03:08.833 --> 00:03:10.833
however attractive

58
00:03:10.833 --> 00:03:13.375
it may seem, can bind the soul.

59
00:03:13.375 --> 00:03:17.083
If the jivatma becomes attached to
its happiness and knowledge,

60
00:03:17.083 --> 00:03:20.333
it remains far from liberation.

61
00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:24.250
The only path to rise above all gunas

62
00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:26.541
is devotion to Lord Krishna.

63
00:03:26.541 --> 00:03:30.333
This devotion alone frees the
soul from material bondage

64
00:03:30.333 --> 00:03:33.916
and leads it toward supreme liberation.

65
00:03:38.333 --> 00:03:40.666
You may feel

66
00:03:40.666 --> 00:03:43.166
you have made progress –

67
00:03:43.166 --> 00:03:46.666
because your life is calm,

68
00:03:46.666 --> 00:03:50.208
your decisions seem better,

69
00:03:50.208 --> 00:03:53.791
and your thinking appears refined.

70
00:03:53.791 --> 00:03:58.958
And yes – sattva Guna brings all of this.

71
00:03:58.958 --> 00:04:01.416
It gives you clarity.

72
00:04:01.416 --> 00:04:04.958
It opens the door to learning.

73
00:04:04.958 --> 00:04:08.916
It makes you experience peace.

74
00:04:08.916 --> 00:04:11.000
But there is something

75
00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:16.583
you may not recognise for a long time –

76
00:04:16.583 --> 00:04:21.583
even the finest gifts of sattva Guna

77
00:04:21.583 --> 00:04:23.791
can bind you,

78
00:04:23.791 --> 00:04:26.875
if you are not careful.

79
00:04:26.875 --> 00:04:28.916
It is often seen

80
00:04:28.916 --> 00:04:32.208
that people give generously,

81
00:04:32.208 --> 00:04:36.083
practise restraint in food and habits –

82
00:04:36.083 --> 00:04:37.208
but then

83
00:04:37.208 --> 00:04:41.375
begin loudly advertising their charity.

84
00:04:41.375 --> 00:04:44.708
They put up large photographs of themselves giving,

85
00:04:44.708 --> 00:04:48.833
at every crossroads in the city.

86
00:04:48.833 --> 00:04:52.000
They may give up the greed for wealth,

87
00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:57.166
but cannot give up the greed to
be called a renunciant.

88
00:04:57.166 --> 00:04:58.666
They remain trapped.

89
00:04:58.666 --> 00:05:02.250
You begin to take pride in your knowledge.

90
00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:02.958
Within,

91
00:05:02.958 --> 00:05:07.083
you start thinking – ‘I am superior to all those

92
00:05:07.083 --> 00:05:11.833
still wandering in life.’

93
00:05:11.833 --> 00:05:16.000
You become attached to the happiness

94
00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:18.708
that comes from goodness,

95
00:05:18.708 --> 00:05:21.875
and overlook the truth –

96
00:05:21.875 --> 00:05:26.416
that you are still bound.

97
00:05:26.416 --> 00:05:28.666
This is the cleverness

98
00:05:28.666 --> 00:05:31.708
of material energy.

99
00:05:31.708 --> 00:05:35.458
It makes you feel elevated,

100
00:05:35.458 --> 00:05:39.166
yet keeps you bound –

101
00:05:39.166 --> 00:05:42.750
because even attachment to light

102
00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:46.000
can become your shadow.

103
00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:49.875
I do not want you to stop growing.

104
00:05:49.875 --> 00:05:54.250
I want you to grow even further.

105
00:05:54.250 --> 00:05:58.041
Let go of pride. Let go of ownership.

106
00:05:58.041 --> 00:06:01.833
Let your goodness be a doorway,

107
00:06:01.833 --> 00:06:04.000
not a bondage.

108
00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:08.958
When you act without attachment to happiness,

109
00:06:08.958 --> 00:06:11.208
only then will you truly walk

110
00:06:11.208 --> 00:06:13.375
the path of freedom –

111
00:06:13.375 --> 00:06:19.166
and on that journey, I will always be with you.

112
00:06:23.791 --> 00:06:25.583
You may

113
00:06:25.583 --> 00:06:29.416
look at your family and feel –

114
00:06:29.416 --> 00:06:31.166
all is well.

115
00:06:31.166 --> 00:06:34.208
We do no harm to anyone.

116
00:06:34.208 --> 00:06:36.541
We live by good values.

117
00:06:36.541 --> 00:06:39.125
We are kind to others.

118
00:06:39.125 --> 00:06:41.541
What more is needed?

119
00:06:41.541 --> 00:06:46.000
But this is exactly where the trap lies –

120
00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:48.458
the trap of self-satisfaction.

121
00:06:48.458 --> 00:06:53.916
It is that quiet voice which says – ‘all is fine,

122
00:06:53.916 --> 00:06:57.875
no need to move further.’

123
00:06:57.875 --> 00:07:02.125
Think of a student

124
00:07:02.125 --> 00:07:08.583
who aims only to pass the exam.

125
00:07:08.583 --> 00:07:09.583
They are

126
00:07:09.583 --> 00:07:11.416
satisfied with the minimum

127
00:07:11.416 --> 00:07:13.625
passing marks.

128
00:07:13.625 --> 00:07:14.750
Perhaps

129
00:07:14.750 --> 00:07:18.375
they had the capacity for full marks,

130
00:07:18.375 --> 00:07:21.541
but this sense of self-satisfaction

131
00:07:21.541 --> 00:07:25.083
at a small goal stops their growth –

132
00:07:25.083 --> 00:07:26.916
and they think,

133
00:07:26.916 --> 00:07:30.500
‘I achieved my goal of passing –

134
00:07:30.500 --> 00:07:33.041
how happy I am!’

135
00:07:33.041 --> 00:07:38.208
Sattva Guna gives you a moral and peaceful life.

136
00:07:38.208 --> 00:07:42.291
But if you stop here,

137
00:07:42.291 --> 00:07:46.083
the inner drive to keep seeking diminishes.

138
00:07:46.083 --> 00:07:50.541
You stop asking deeper questions.

139
00:07:50.541 --> 00:07:53.666
You even reduce your reaching toward Me.

140
00:07:53.666 --> 00:07:55.833
Life remains good,

141
00:07:55.833 --> 00:07:58.750
but spiritual awakening does not happen.

142
00:07:58.750 --> 00:08:02.166
Many families stop right here.

143
00:08:02.166 --> 00:08:05.916
They become so cultured and refined

144
00:08:05.916 --> 00:08:11.166
that they feel the journey is complete.

145
00:08:11.166 --> 00:08:13.000
But in truth,

146
00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:17.000
this is only the first step.

147
00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:23.000
Do not let your family settle into this stillness.

148
00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:25.541
Make your goodness a stepping stone,

149
00:08:25.541 --> 00:08:27.833
not a final stop.

150
00:08:27.833 --> 00:08:31.000
Encourage spiritual conversation.

151
00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:32.833
Make time –

152
00:08:32.833 --> 00:08:34.583
to hear My name,

153
00:08:34.583 --> 00:08:36.291
to do japa,

154
00:08:36.291 --> 00:08:39.000
and to serve together.

155
00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:42.666
A good life is a gift.

156
00:08:42.666 --> 00:08:46.666
But a spiritual life is a calling.

157
00:08:46.666 --> 00:08:52.416
Do not lose it by settling for merely ‘fine.’

158
00:08:52.416 --> 00:08:54.208
I want

159
00:08:54.208 --> 00:08:57.916
your family not only to be at peace,

160
00:08:57.916 --> 00:09:02.625
but to be awakened – and to move
beyond even sattva

161
00:09:02.625 --> 00:09:05.666
toward liberation.

162
00:09:10.291 --> 00:09:11.833
Many people

163
00:09:11.833 --> 00:09:14.083
rise to great heights

164
00:09:14.083 --> 00:09:16.625
through their intellect.

165
00:09:16.625 --> 00:09:20.041
They read more, know more,

166
00:09:20.041 --> 00:09:23.291
and speak with clarity.

167
00:09:23.291 --> 00:09:25.291
But gradually

168
00:09:25.291 --> 00:09:27.875
a shift comes.

169
00:09:27.875 --> 00:09:31.000
They begin to believe that they

170
00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:34.333
themselves are their knowledge.

171
00:09:34.333 --> 00:09:37.541
They listen less.

172
00:09:37.541 --> 00:09:43.000
They think – ‘I already know this.’

173
00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:45.875
This is where growth slows…

174
00:09:45.875 --> 00:09:49.208
and eventually stops.

175
00:09:49.208 --> 00:09:53.333
This is why I say –

176
00:09:53.333 --> 00:09:57.375
knowledge too, when joined with ego,

177
00:09:57.375 --> 00:10:00.875
becomes a rope that binds.

178
00:10:00.875 --> 00:10:05.375
When intelligence becomes your identity,

179
00:10:05.375 --> 00:10:10.000
you begin to judge others

180
00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:13.541
by what they do not know,

181
00:10:13.541 --> 00:10:17.791
when instead you should be celebrating

182
00:10:17.791 --> 00:10:23.958
the new opportunity to learn something
fresh together with everyone.

183
00:10:23.958 --> 00:10:29.000
When the veil of knowledge-ego
covers your vision,

184
00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:32.708
you can no longer see the vastness

185
00:10:32.708 --> 00:10:35.958
that still remains unknown.

186
00:10:35.958 --> 00:10:39.666
At the workplace this often shows up as –

187
00:10:39.666 --> 00:10:42.375
not accepting feedback,

188
00:10:42.375 --> 00:10:44.583
resisting a new perspective,

189
00:10:44.583 --> 00:10:48.708
or a quiet sense of superiority.

190
00:10:48.708 --> 00:10:52.083
But true knowledge makes you humble

191
00:10:52.083 --> 00:10:54.791
and gentle.

192
00:10:54.791 --> 00:10:58.041
Because the more you know,

193
00:10:58.041 --> 00:11:01.875
the more you realise how much still

194
00:11:01.875 --> 00:11:04.041
remains to be known.

195
00:11:04.041 --> 00:11:07.125
As an employee –

196
00:11:07.125 --> 00:11:10.000
if your days pass only doing

197
00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:11.625
the minimum needed

198
00:11:11.625 --> 00:11:13.041
to collect your salary

199
00:11:13.041 --> 00:11:16.500
on the first of the month,

200
00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:18.708
there will be no growth.

201
00:11:18.708 --> 00:11:20.916
The desire to keep learning

202
00:11:20.916 --> 00:11:23.875
opens new paths of progress.

203
00:11:23.875 --> 00:11:24.916
So do not let

204
00:11:24.916 --> 00:11:26.833
your intelligence become

205
00:11:26.833 --> 00:11:29.666
your ceiling.

206
00:11:29.666 --> 00:11:31.541
Stay curious.

207
00:11:31.541 --> 00:11:33.791
Keep learning with an open mind.

208
00:11:33.791 --> 00:11:37.750
Use your knowledge to create space for others –

209
00:11:37.750 --> 00:11:40.666
not to overshadow them.

210
00:11:40.666 --> 00:11:43.500
The highest knowledge does not say –

211
00:11:43.500 --> 00:11:45.500
‘I know more.’

212
00:11:45.500 --> 00:11:49.833
It says – ‘I am always learning.’

213
00:11:49.833 --> 00:11:52.291
This is true progress.

214
00:11:52.291 --> 00:11:54.541
This is true leadership.
